    "done_when": "A new module reckon/crew/repair.py turns one stored review record into exactly one repair node, as the reuse map at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s25-coord/s25-reuse-map-review-reflex/reuse-map.md row 1 and node B describe. The node's brief lists every finding with a stable finding id. Its write scope is the union of the paths the findings name plus the reviewed run's own fence, so a finding outside that fence is granted rather than refused. Its manifest contract asks the repair to answer each finding it declines with a reason. A redispatch of that repair is another attempt of the same round, not a second round. The module imports the existing review parser and store and edits neither; reckon/crew/review.py and reckon/crew/recovery.py are held by other nodes and are not touched. tests/test_review_findings_compose_a_repair.py drives a stored review with three findings, one naming a path outside the reviewed run's fence, and asserts four things: one repair node composed; its brief naming all three findings by id; its write scope containing the out-of-fence path; and a second composition for the same round returning the same node rather than a new one. It passes at exit 0. The manifest records base and head arms in the armed JSON form with FAILED ids, and the head arm is run at the committed head. The declared negative control is applied, the three-finding case is observed to fail, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED test id. Wiring the composer into the review reflex is a later node, because the reflex's file is held.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
